srow(44, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL PUT THESE MY WORDS ON YOUR HEART" (11:18) — THIS IS THE STUDY OF TORAH; "AND BIND THEM FOR A SIGN ON YOUR HAND" — THESE ARE THE TEFILLIN. ONLY TEFILLIN AND STUDY? THE OTHER COMMANDMENTS — BY THE COMMON GROUND OF THE TWO: TEFILLIN IS NOT LIKE STUDY NOR STUDY LIKE TEFILLIN, BUT BOTH ARE DUTIES OF THE BODY NOT BOUND TO THE LAND, PRACTISED IN THE LAND AND ABROAD — SO EVERY DUTY OF THE BODY; AND THE LAND-BOUND ONLY IN THE LAND, EXCEPT ORLAH AND MIXED KINDS; R. ELIEZER: THE NEW GRAIN TOO. The head row of piska 44 — THE RULE OF THE LAND-BOUND ({SP_(44, 1, "זה", "תלמוד", "תורה")} "this is the study of Torah"; {SP_(44, 1, "אלו", "תפלין")} "these are tefillin"; {SP_(44, 1, "מבנין", "אב", "שבין", "שניהם")} "from the common ground of the two"; {SP_(44, 1, "מצוות", "הגוף", "שאין", "תלויות", "בארץ")} "duties of the body not bound to the land"; {SP_(44, 1, "חוץ", "מן", "הערלה", "והכלאים")} "except orlah and mixed kinds"): I3 (binyan av from two verses — checked; Kiddushin 37a the docket\'s; Mishnah Kiddushin 1:9 in the note) — THE PARTITION OF THE COMMANDMENTS BY THE LAND, a DATA row for the compile (40:5\'s dues the land-bound side; 43:34\'s exile the other). Fresh in both files.')
srow(45, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL PUT THESE MY WORDS ON YOUR HEART" — WORDS OF TORAH ARE LIKENED TO A LIFE-GIVING POTION: THE KING WHO STRUCK HIS SON AND LAID A DRESSING ON THE WOUND — WHILE IT IS ON YOU EAT, DRINK AND BATHE AS YOU PLEASE; LIFT IT AND THE WOUND FESTERS. SO THE HOLY ONE: MY SONS, I CREATED THE EVIL INCLINATION AND NOTHING IS WORSE — "IF YOU DO WELL, IT IS LIFTED" (GENESIS 4:7): BUSY YOURSELVES WITH TORAH AND IT DOES NOT RULE YOU; LEAVE TORAH AND IT RULES YOU — "SIN CROUCHES AT THE DOOR"; BUT "YOU CAN RULE OVER IT"; "IF YOUR ENEMY HUNGERS, FEED HIM" (PROVERBS 25:21-22). THE INCLINATION IS EVIL — ITS MAKER TESTIFIES: "THE INCLINATION OF MAN\'S HEART IS EVIL" (GENESIS 8:21). The potion ({SP_(45, 1, "שנמשלו", "דברי", "תורה", "בסם", "חיים")} "that words of Torah are likened to a potion of life"; {SP_(45, 1, "בראתי", "לכם", "יצר", "הרע")} "I created for you the evil inclination"): E26 (checked); THE PISKA WITHOUT A HEAD CITATION — its one row opens with 11:18\'s words (asserted; the head regex finds none), the spine\'s; the Proverbs range citation invisible to the regex (asserted); the inclination\'s name chapter 10\'s (the docket\'s Sukkah 52a). Read before at two Genesis sittings (gen_12 Cain and Abel, gen_20), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(46, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL TEACH THEM TO YOUR SONS" (11:19) — YOUR SONS AND NOT YOUR DAUGHTERS: R. YOSE BEN AKIVA. HENCE THEY SAID: WHEN THE CHILD BEGINS TO SPEAK, HIS FATHER SPEAKS WITH HIM IN THE HOLY TONGUE AND TEACHES HIM TORAH; IF NOT, IT IS AS IF HE BURIED HIM — "TEACH THEM TO YOUR SONS TO SPEAK OF THEM": IF YOU TEACH — "THAT YOUR DAYS BE MULTIPLIED" (11:21); IF NOT — THAT YOUR DAYS BE SHORTENED, FOR SO WORDS OF TORAH ARE EXPOUNDED: FROM THE YES THE NO, FROM THE NO THE YES. The sons ({SP_(46, 1, "בניכם", "ולא", "בנותיכם")} "your sons and not your daughters"; {SP_(46, 1, "מכלל", "הן", "לאו", "ומכלל", "לאו", "הן")} "from the yes the no and from the no the yes"): "sons" read to exclude daughters (Mishnah Sotah 3:4 in the note; Kiddushin 29b the docket\'s), the holy tongue from the first words (the Tosefta Hagigah 1:2), the affirmation implying its negation (the Mekhilta Bahodesh 8 — named, no code); the row cites 11:19 and 11:21 (the two verses in one row — asserted). Fresh.')
srow(47, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT YOUR DAYS BE MULTIPLIED" (11:21) — IN THIS WORLD; "AND THE DAYS OF YOUR SONS" — IN THE DAYS OF THE MESSIAH. The head row of piska 47 ({SP_(47, 1, "בעולם", "הזה")} "in this world"; {SP_(47, 1, "לימות", "המשיח")} "in the days of the Messiah"): the verse\'s three clauses three ages (47:2 the third). Fresh.')
srow(47, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS THE DAYS OF THE HEAVENS ABOVE THE EARTH" — THE WORLD TO COME. "WHICH THE LORD SWORE TO YOUR FATHERS TO GIVE TO YOU" IS NOT WRITTEN BUT "TO GIVE TO THEM": WE LEARN THE RESURRECTION OF THE DEAD FROM THE TORAH. THE RESURRECTION FROM "TO THEM" ({SP_(47, 2, "לתת", "להם")} "to give to them"; {SP_(47, 2, "תחית", "המתים", "מן", "התורה")} "the resurrection of the dead from the Torah"): the suffix read — the fathers themselves the recipients (Sanhedrin 90b the docket\'s); the ink: "to give to them" 11:9 and 11:21 (computed). Fresh.')
srow(47, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AS THE DAYS OF THE HEAVENS ABOVE THE EARTH" — THAT THE FACES OF THE RIGHTEOUS BE AS THE DAY: "THOSE WHO LOVE HIM AS THE SUN GOING FORTH IN ITS MIGHT" (JUDGES 5:31); R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: SEVEN JOYS THE FACES OF THE RIGHTEOUS WILL GREET THE PRESENCE WITH — THE SUN, THE MOON (SONG 6:10), THE FIRMAMENT AND THE STARS (DANIEL 12:3), THE LIGHTNING (NAHUM 2:5), THE LILIES (PSALM 45:1), THE OLIVE (HOSEA 14:7). ({SP_(47, 3, "לשבע", "שמחות")} "to seven joys"). Fresh.')
srow(47, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"A SONG FOR THE ASCENTS" (PSALM 121:1) — FOR HIM WHO WILL MAKE ASCENTS FOR HIS RIGHTEOUS SERVANTS. R. AKIVA: NOT "A SONG FOR THE ASCENT" BUT "FOR THE ASCENTS" — THIRTY ASCENTS ONE ABOVE ANOTHER; RABBI: SIXTY. OR IS THERE ENMITY AND ENVY AMONG THEM? "THOSE WHO MAKE MANY RIGHTEOUS ARE AS THE STARS" (DANIEL 12:3): AS THE STARS HAVE NO ENMITY, SO THE RIGHTEOUS; AS NO STAR\'S LIGHT IS ANOTHER\'S, SO THE RIGHTEOUS. The thirty and the sixty ({SP_(47, 4, "שלשים", "מעלות", "זו", "למעלה", "מזו")} "thirty ascents one above another"; {SP_(47, 4, "ששים", "מעלות")} "sixty ascents"): E29 (gematria — the preposition\'s letter-value thirty, doubled by the plural — checked; the English\'s note the computation). Fresh.')
srow(47, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "THOSE WHO MAKE MANY RIGHTEOUS" — THE CHARITY COLLECTORS; R. SHIMON BEN MENASYA: THE ELDERS — "THOSE WHO LOVE HIM AS THE SUN": WHO IS GREATER, THE LOVERS OR THOSE WHO MAKE OTHERS LOVE? IF THE LOVERS ARE AS THE SUN, HOW MUCH MORE THOSE WHO MAKE LOVE. ({SP_(47, 5, "אלו", "גבאי", "צדקה")} "these are the charity collectors"; {SP_(47, 5, "הוי", "אומר", "המאהיבים")} "say: those who make others love"); I1 (checked). Fresh.')
srow(47, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"AS THE STARS FOR EVER AND EVER" — AS THE STARS ARE HIGH OVER ALL, RULE FROM END TO END, HIDDEN AND REVEALED, IN COMPANIES BEYOND COUNT — SO THE RIGHTEOUS; WHETHER THEY DO HIS WILL OR NOT? "YOUR SEED SHALL BE AS THE DUST OF THE EARTH" (GENESIS 28:14): DOING HIS WILL, STARS; NOT, DUST — "THE KING OF ARAM MADE THEM AS DUST TO TRAMPLE" (2 KINGS 13:7). ({SP_(47, 6, "כתות", "כתות", "שאין", "להם", "מנין")} "companies upon companies without number"). Fresh.')
srow(47, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AS THE DAYS OF THE HEAVENS ABOVE THE EARTH" — THAT THEY LIVE AND STAND FOR EVER AND EVER, "AS THE NEW HEAVENS" (ISAIAH 66:22): IF HEAVEN AND EARTH, CREATED ONLY FOR ISRAEL\'S HONOR, STAND FOR EVER, HOW MUCH MORE THE RIGHTEOUS, FOR WHOM THE WORLD WAS CREATED. ({SP_(47, 7, "חיים", "וקימים", "לעולם")} "living and standing for ever"); I1 (checked). Fresh.')
srow(47, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: "AS THE DAYS OF THE TREE ARE THE DAYS OF MY PEOPLE" (ISAIAH 65:22) — THE TREE IS THE TORAH, "A TREE OF LIFE TO THOSE WHO HOLD IT" (PROVERBS 3:18): IF THE TORAH, CREATED FOR ISRAEL\'S HONOR, STANDS FOR EVER, HOW MUCH MORE THE RIGHTEOUS. ({SP_(47, 8, "ואין", "עץ", "אלא", "תורה")} "and the tree is nothing but Torah"); I1 (checked). Fresh.')
srow(47, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JOSHUA BEN KORHAH: "A GENERATION GOES AND A GENERATION COMES, AND THE EARTH STANDS FOR EVER" (ECCLESIASTES 1:4) — READ RATHER "THE EARTH GOES AND THE EARTH COMES, AND A GENERATION STANDS FOR EVER"; BECAUSE THEY CHANGED THEIR DEEDS, THE ALL-PRESENT CHANGED THE WORLD\'S ORDER ON THEM. "AND THE NUMBER OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL SHALL BE" (HOSEA 2:1) AND "AS THE SAND OF THE SEA WHICH CANNOT BE MEASURED": DOING HIS WILL — AS THE SAND; NOT — "THE NUMBER"; ISAIAH 30:17, AMOS 5:3. ANOTHER WORD: "THE NUMBER" — THE NUMBER OF HEAVEN; "AS THE SAND" — THE NUMBER OF MAN. The two numbers ({SP_(47, 9, "זה", "מספר", "שמים")} "this is heaven\'s number"; {SP_(47, 9, "זה", "מספר", "אדם")} "this is man\'s number"): the verse\'s two halves read as a condition and as two counts — heaven\'s and man\'s (the census\'s DATA: the count uncountable when Israel does His will; the population layer\'s question); no code. Fresh.')
srow(48, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR IF YOU KEEP DILIGENTLY ALL THIS COMMANDMENT" (11:22) — WHY SAID? SINCE "IF YOU HEARKEN DILIGENTLY TO MY COMMANDMENTS" (11:13), MIGHT ONE HEAR WORDS OF TORAH AND SIT WITHOUT REPEATING? "IF YOU KEEP DILIGENTLY": AS A MAN GUARDS HIS COIN FROM LOSS, SO HIS LEARNING — "IF YOU SEEK IT AS SILVER" (PROVERBS 2:4): AS SILVER IS HARD TO GAIN, SO WORDS OF TORAH; OR HARD TO LOSE? "GOLD AND GLASS CANNOT EQUAL IT" (JOB 28:17): HARD TO GAIN AS GOLD, EASY TO LOSE AS GLASS. The head row of piska 48 ({SP_(48, 1, "להזהר", "בסלעו", "שלא", "תאבד")} "to guard his coin that it be not lost"; {SP_(48, 1, "קשים", "לקנותם", "כזהב", "ונוחים", "לאבדם")} "hard to gain as gold and easy to lose"): the chapter\'s two doubled infinitives paired by the shelf (11:13 "hearken, hearken" / 11:22 "keep, keep" — the ink\'s two infinitive absolutes); 11:13 cited by name in the piska on 11:22 (asserted). Fresh in both files.')
srow(48, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YISHMAEL: "ONLY TAKE HEED TO YOURSELF AND KEEP YOUR SOUL DILIGENTLY" (4:9) — THE KING WHO CAUGHT A BIRD AND GAVE IT TO HIS SERVANT: GUARD IT FOR MY SON — IF YOU LOSE IT, DO NOT THINK YOU LOST A PENNY\'S BIRD BUT YOUR LIFE; "IT IS NO EMPTY THING FOR YOU" (32:47) — THE THING YOU CALL EMPTY IS YOUR LIFE. The bird ({SP_(48, 2, "משל", "למלך", "בשר", "ודם", "שצד", "צפור")} "a parable of a king of flesh and blood who caught a bird"; {SP_(48, 2, "הוא", "חייכם")} "it is your life"): E26 (checked); 4:9 the row\'s seat at chapter 4 (read there, reread whole here). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(48, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: TWO BROTHERS HEIRS OF THEIR FATHER — ONE MELTS A DENAR AND EATS IT, ONE MELTS A DENAR AND LAYS IT BY: THE FIRST HAS NOTHING, THE SECOND GROWS RICH IN TIME. SO THE DISCIPLES: TWO OR THREE THINGS A DAY, TWO OR THREE CHAPTERS A WEEK, TWO OR THREE PORTIONS A MONTH — RICH IN TIME, "HE WHO GATHERS BY HAND INCREASES" (PROVERBS 13:11); HE WHO SAYS "TODAY I LEARN, TOMORROW I LEARN" HAS NOTHING (10:5, 20:4; ECCLESIASTES 11:4); "I PASSED THE FIELD OF THE SLUGGARD" (PROVERBS 24:30-31) — HE HAD A FIELD AND A VINEYARD AND DID NOT LABOR IN THEM; HE FORGETS TWO OR THREE THINGS OF THE PORTION, SEEKS ITS OPENING AND FINDS IT NOT, ITS WALL IS BROKEN — HE SITS, DECLARES THE CLEAN UNCLEAN AND THE UNCLEAN CLEAN AND BREAKS THE SAGES\' FENCE: "HE WHO BREAKS A FENCE, A SERPENT BITES HIM" (ECCLESIASTES 10:8). The two brothers ({SP_(48, 3, "משל", "לשני", "אחים")} "a parable of two brothers"; {SP_(48, 3, "ופורץ", "גדר", "ישכנו", "נחש")} "and he who breaks a fence, a serpent bites him"): E26 (checked); the sages\' fence (Avot 1:1 in the note). Fresh.')
srow(48, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON BEN MENASYA: "THE SATED SOUL TRAMPLES HONEY" (PROVERBS 27:7) — THE DISCIPLE WHO AT FIRST LEARNED EVERYTHING; ANOTHER WORD: AS THE SIEVE (NAFAH) PUTS OUT THE FLOUR, THE BRAN AND THE COARSE MEAL EACH BY ITSELF, SO THE DISCIPLE SITS AND SORTS WORDS OF TORAH — SO-AND-SO FORBIDS, SO-AND-SO PERMITS. ({SP_(48, 4, "תלמיד", "מתחלתו", "למד", "כל", "דבר")} "a disciple who at first learned everything"); the sound-play honey / sieve named. Fresh.')
srow(48, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: THE STRONG DISCIPLE IS A SPONGE, ABSORBING ALL; THE NEXT A RAG, ABSORBING ONLY ITS NEED — "ENOUGH WHAT MY MASTER TAUGHT ME". R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: "DRINK WATER FROM YOUR OWN CISTERN" (PROVERBS 5:15) — LEARN FROM WHO IS WITH YOU IN THE CITY, THEN SET OUT EVERYWHERE (31:14). R. SHIMON BEN MENASYA: DRINK THE WATERS OF YOUR CREATOR, NOT MUDDY WATERS DRAWN AFTER THE HERETICS. R. AKIVA: A WELL AT FIRST CANNOT GIVE A DROP OF ITSELF; "STREAMS FROM YOUR WELL" (5:15-16) — LIVING WATER FROM EVERY SIDE, DISCIPLES COME AND LEARN. WORDS OF TORAH ARE LIKENED TO WATER: LIFE TO THE WORLD (4:22), RAISING THE UNCLEAN (PSALM 119:140), RESTORING THE SOUL (PROVERBS 25:25; PSALM 19:8), FREE TO THE WORLD (ISAIAH 55:1), PRICELESS (PROVERBS 3:15). The water ({SP_(48, 5, "דומה", "לספוג")} "like a sponge"; {SP_(48, 5, "נמשלו", "דברי", "תורה", "למים")} "words of Torah are likened to water"): the sound-play cistern / Creator named (Avot 5:15 and 1:11 in the notes); no code. Fresh.')
srow(48, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'OR AS WATER DOES NOT GLADDEN THE HEART, WORDS OF TORAH DO NOT? "YOUR LOVE IS BETTER THAN WINE" (SONG 1:2): AS WINE GLADDENS THE HEART (PSALM 19:9), AS WINE IMPROVES WITH AGE IN THE JAR (JOB 12:12), AS WINE KEEPS ONLY IN EARTHENWARE — SO WORDS OF TORAH IN HIM WHO IS EARTHENWARE IN HIS OWN EYES. ({SP_(48, 6, "מה", "יין", "משמח", "את", "הלב")} "as wine gladdens the heart"). Fresh.')
srow(48, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'OR AS WINE IS SOMETIMES BAD FOR HEAD AND BODY? "YOUR OILS ARE GOOD FOR FRAGRANCE" (SONG 1:3): AS OIL IS GOOD FOR HEAD AND BODY, SO WORDS OF TORAH (PROVERBS 1:9, 4:9) — LIKENED TO OIL AND HONEY, "SWEETER THAN HONEY" (PSALM 19:11). ({SP_(48, 7, "נמשלו", "דברי", "תורה", "בשמן", "ודבש")} "words of Torah are likened to oil and honey"). Fresh.')
srow(48, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "IF YOU KEEP DILIGENTLY" — IF A MAN HEARS WORDS OF TORAH FIRST BY FIRST AND KEEPS THEM, AS THE FIRST STAND IN HIS HAND SO THE LAST; AND IF HE HEARS FIRST BY FIRST AND FORGETS, AS THE FIRST DO NOT STAND SO THE LAST — "IF YOU FORGET, FORGET" (8:19): LIFT YOUR EYES FROM IT AND IT IS GONE (PROVERBS 23:5); AND IN THE SCROLL OF THE PIOUS: "LEAVE ME A DAY AND I WILL LEAVE YOU TWO". The two doublings ({SP_(48, 8, "ראשון", "ראשון", "ומקימו")} "first by first and keeps them"; {SP_(48, 8, "יום", "תעזבני", "יומים", "אעזבך")} "leave Me a day, I will leave you two days"): 11:22\'s "keep, keep" against 8:19\'s "forget, forget" — chapter 8\'s row (E10 typed there on the doubled verb; read there and reread whole here); the scroll\'s name the English discusses at length (read, marked). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(48, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "IF YOU KEEP DILIGENTLY" — LEST YOU SAY, THE SONS OF THE ELDERS, OF THE GREAT, OF THE PROPHETS STUDY — "IF YOU KEEP": ALL ARE EQUAL IN THE TORAH, "THE TORAH MOSES COMMANDED US, THE HERITAGE OF THE CONGREGATION OF JACOB" (33:4) — NOT PRIESTS, LEVITES AND ISRAELITES BUT "THE CONGREGATION OF JACOB"; "YOU STAND TODAY, ALL OF YOU" (29:9); HAD SHAPHAN NOT STOOD IN HIS HOUR, EZRA IN HIS, R. AKIVA IN HIS, THE TORAH WOULD HAVE BEEN FORGOTTEN — "A WORD IN ITS SEASON, HOW GOOD" (PROVERBS 15:23). "THEY SHALL RUN TO SEEK THE WORD OF THE LORD AND NOT FIND IT" (AMOS 8:12) — OUR MASTERS PERMITTED GOING FROM CITY TO CITY OVER A CREEPING THING THAT TOUCHED A LOAF, TO KNOW IF IT IS FIRST OR SECOND DEGREE; R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: SHALL THE TORAH BE FORGOTTEN? "IT SHALL NOT BE FORGOTTEN FROM THE MOUTH OF HIS SEED" (31:21) — RATHER, SO-AND-SO FORBIDS, SO-AND-SO PERMITS, AND THEY FIND NO CLEAR WORD. All equal in the Torah ({SP_(48, 9, "שהכל", "שוים", "בתורה")} "that all are equal in the Torah"; {SP_(48, 9, "ולא", "ימצאו", "דבר", "ברור")} "and they will not find a clear word"): the Tosefta Eduyot 1:1 in the note; 33:4, 29:9 and 31:21 by CALL ahead (the song\'s oath). Fresh.')
srow(48, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "IF YOU KEEP DILIGENTLY" — LEST YOU SAY, I LEARN THE HARD PORTION AND LEAVE THE EASY: "IT IS NO EMPTY THING FOR YOU" (32:47); LEST YOU SAY, I HAVE LEARNED LAWS, ENOUGH: "THE COMMANDMENT", "THE COMMANDMENT", "ALL THE COMMANDMENT" — LEARN MIDRASH, LAWS AND LORE; "NOT BY BREAD ALONE DOES MAN LIVE" (8:3) — THIS IS MIDRASH; "BY ALL THAT PROCEEDS FROM THE MOUTH OF THE LORD" — LAWS AND LORE; "BE WISE, MY SON" (PROVERBS 27:11), "MY HEART TOO WILL REJOICE" (23:15); R. SHIMON BEN MENASYA: "TOO" — TO INCLUDE HIS FATHER IN HEAVEN. The three "commandment"s ({SP_(48, 10, "המצוה", "המצוה", "כל", "המצוה")} "the commandment, the commandment, all the commandment"; {SP_(48, 10, "למוד", "מדרש", "הלכות", "והגדות")} "learn midrash, laws and lore"): E1 (the extension by "all" — checked; the ink: "all the commandment" the singular eight in the book); chapter 8\'s row on 8:3 (read there, reread whole here); "too" the second extension (E1\'s "gam" — checked). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(48, 11, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH I COMMAND YOU TO DO IT" — WHY SAID? SINCE "IF YOU KEEP DILIGENTLY", MIGHT ONE KEEP WORDS OF TORAH AND SIT WITHOUT DOING? "TO DO IT": ITS ANSWER IS TO DO IT — LEARNED, ONE COMMANDMENT IN HAND; LEARNED AND KEPT, TWO; LEARNED, KEPT AND DID — NONE ABOVE HIM. ({SP_(48, 11, "תשובתה", "לעשתה")} "its answer: to do it"; {SP_(48, 11, "אין", "למעלה", "הימנו")} "none above him"); the ink: "to do it" 11:22 and 19:9 (computed). Fresh.')
srow(48, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO LOVE" — LEST YOU SAY, I LEARN TORAH TO BE CALLED A SAGE, TO SIT IN THE ACADEMY, TO PROLONG DAYS IN THE WORLD TO COME: "TO LOVE" — LEARN IN ANY CASE, AND THE HONOR WILL COME (PROVERBS 3:18, 4:22, 4:9 — THE WREATH IN THIS WORLD, THE CROWN IN THE NEXT; 3:16 — LENGTH OF DAYS IN THE NEXT, RICHES AND HONOR IN THIS). R. ELAZAR SON OF R. ZADOK: DO THINGS FOR THEIR OWN SAKE, SPEAK OF THEM FOR THEIR OWN SAKE; IF BELSHAZZAR, WHO USED THE TEMPLE\'S VESSELS — PROFANE VESSELS — WAS UPROOTED FROM BOTH WORLDS, HOW MUCH MORE HE WHO USES THE VESSEL BY WHICH THE WORLD WAS CREATED. The love of the study ({SP_(48, 12, "למוד", "מכל", "מקום", "וסוף", "הכבוד", "לבוא")} "learn in any case, and the honor will come in the end"): 41:16\'s rule on 11:13 said again on 11:22 (the shelf reading the two "to love"s as one — the ink\'s two seats); I1 (checked) from Belshazzar\'s vessels (Avot 3:14 in the note). Fresh.')

